<title>USA: Plaintiffs, creditors seek Dow Corning settlement.</title>
<headline>Plaintiffs, creditors seek Dow Corning settlement.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON</dateline>
<text>
<p>Women suing Dow Corning Corp. for alleged harm from the company's silicone breast implants and its commercial creditors Friday proposed that Dow Corning provide about $2.95 billion to settle their claims.</p>
<p>The proposal was made under a reorganization plan that the groups drew up for Dow Corning to emerge from Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection. The groups said they asked for court approval to file the plan with the U.S. Bankruptcy Court in Bay City, Mich.</p>
</text>
